.TH DEVOS 1 "2026" "DevOS" "DevOS Manual"
.SH NAME
devos \- DevOS reproducibility engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B devos
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
devos manages reproducible DevOps toolchains via declarative profiles and lockfiles.
It runs unprivileged; privileged steps use per-operation elevation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Report environment facts (no changes).
.TP
.B profile list|inspect|validate NAME
List, print, or validate profiles.
.TP
.B profile apply NAME [--confirm] [--ask-become-pass]
Install a profile (dry-run unless --confirm). Pins to the lockfile when present.
.TP
.B profile remove NAME [--confirm]
Remove a profile's packages (preserves user data).
.TP
.B profile lock NAME
Resolve installed versions into locks/NAME.lock.json.
.TP
.B profile rollback NAME [--to FILE] [--confirm]
Reinstall exact versions from a lockfile.
.TP
.B drift check --profile NAME
Report declared-vs-installed drift (no changes).
.TP
.B update [--system]
Report available tool (or whole-OS) updates. Read-only.
.TP
.B tools list --profile NAME
List managed tool versions.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 ok, 1 validation failure, 2 usage, 3 not found, 4 engine error, 5 provisioning failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project: https://github.com/sayaksatpathi/DEVOPS-OS
